<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  EVB battlesuit types for Infall: Deck Collapse. An EVB Dock holds up to 4 suit types, like a weapon system holds
  weapons (heromedel 2026-10-29). Each suit type adds "speed" Launch cards. The dock's level is the power it can
  spend on launches each turn, and a suit's turns of air and ammo: level + 1. A launch needs a free crew member in
  the dock, who flies out in the suit, and costs the suit's power. The suit drifts beside a random enemy system
  each turn and acts there; the player doesn't aim it. When its air is gone it stops, and its pilot takes a wound
  each turn until it is recalled (click it, then Recall). The first hit damages a suit and wounds its pilot: it
  can't act and heads home. A second hit destroys it and its pilot (race-profiles.md, Mecha, 2026-10-23, Likely).

  action  shoot      fires at the system it is beside as each of its captain's turns ends (shots, damage, shields, ion)
          intercept  stays by its own ship: shoots down the first enemy torpedo each enemy turn, and fires at an
                     enemy suit each turn
          repair     stays by its own ship: repairs 1 damage on the most damaged system as each turn ends
          board      clings to the system it reached: it and the hull take 1 damage as each enemy turn ends
  speed   Launch cards it adds to the deck (Ai-Generated-Proposal values)
  sortie  Mawjig per turn out when Ammo uses Mawjig; a launch pays for every turn of air (mawjig-cost-table.md:
          laser 0.02, beam 0.03, ion +0.02 per shot; heromedel: a 2-shot suit out for 3 turns pays 6 shots).
          Worked out by the game for shooting and guardian suits; given here for the others (repair: 0.11 a repair).
  launch  Mawjig paid once per launch on top (boarding: 0.08, missile 0.05 + breach 0.03, drone-prices.md; each
          turn's hit inside 0.02, so 3 turns cost 0.14 in all; Infall: Eco 2026-10-29)
  price   Mawjig, priced as the matching drone (docs/reference/drone-prices.md, x 0.242)
-->
<suits>
  <suit id="assault" name="Assault Suit" cost="2" speed="2" action="shoot" shots="2" damage="1" shields="pop" price="12.11">
    Fires 2 bolts at the system it drifts beside as each of your turns ends.
  </suit>
  <!-- The Mecha laser battlesuit (Ship Design's G17): one HalfMech in a suit with a 1-damage arm laser. Price from
       Infall: Eco (2026-10-29): the 2-power laser suit's 12.11 less one power bar at 4.09 (weapon-budget-table.md). -->
  <suit id="laser" name="Laser Suit" cost="1" speed="2" action="shoot" shots="1" damage="1" shields="pop" price="8.02">
    Fires a laser bolt at the system it drifts beside as each of your turns ends.
  </suit>
  <suit id="ion" name="Ion Suit" cost="2" speed="2" action="shoot" shots="1" damage="0" shields="pop" ion="true" price="12.11">
    Fires an ion charge at the system it drifts beside as each of your turns ends.
  </suit>
  <suit id="cutter" name="Cutter Suit" cost="2" speed="2" action="shoot" shots="1" damage="2" shields="reduce" neverMisses="true" price="12.11">
    Sweeps a 2 damage beam over the system it drifts beside as each of your turns ends. Shield layers cut its damage.
  </suit>
  <suit id="guardian" name="Guardian Suit" cost="2" speed="1" action="intercept" price="12.11">
    Stays by your ship: shoots down the first enemy torpedo each enemy turn, and fires at enemy battlesuits.
  </suit>
  <suit id="repair" name="Repair Suit" cost="1" speed="1" action="repair" sortie="0.11" price="7.26">
    Repairs 1 damage on your most damaged system as each of your turns ends.
  </suit>
  <suit id="boarder" name="Boarding Suit" cost="3" speed="1" action="board" launch="0.08" sortie="0.02" price="16.94">
    Bores into the system it reaches. It and the hull take 1 damage as each enemy turn ends.
  </suit>
</suits>
